# patch-01 — batched MTP accept-prefill (generator/generator.py, iterate_gen)
#
# What: replace the per-job `draft_model.prefill` calls in the MTP accept path
#   (one call per job with accepted_length > 1, ~6-8 calls/step at c8/d1, ~24
#   launches each) with one batched prefill over all such jobs. Rows keep their
#   own block table and start position (cache_seqlens = pre-verify kv_position
#   + 1), which the paged attention path already supports per row, so no layout
#   change is needed.
#
#   - Served (non-windowed) draft cache: a single call whose width is the widest
#     accepted length. Shorter rows are padded with their own rejected draft
#     columns; the extra K/V lands at positions at/past the row's committed end
#     (dead slots, overwritten before any read can reach them -- the same
#     lifecycle the verify pass's rejected-position K/V already follows).
#   - EXL3_MTP_KV_WINDOW: the slot block-table row is a ring that aliases
#     positions one cycle apart, so padding past a row's committed end could
#     evict a still-readable committed row. Rows are grouped by accepted length
#     instead and each group runs at its exact width; the written positions are
#     identical to the per-job calls'. Worst case equals today's call count,
#     never worse.
#
#   Rewound (banned-string) jobs are excluded from the batch exactly as they are
#   excluded today, and mtp_last_hidden updates are unchanged. Initial job-join
#   prefill (job.py) and trunk prefill are untouched.
#
# Apply: `patch -p2` from the package dir (the directory containing
#   `exllamav3_ext/`). Verified to apply cleanly against this tree and to
#   produce exactly the intended file.
#
# Estimated saving: ~(J-1) * ~24 launches per decode step where J is the number
#   of jobs with accepted_length > 1 (~-120..-170 launches/step at c8/d1 with
#   typical acceptance), plus ~4-6 small host-side gathers/copies and one
#   device-side row gather on target_hidden.

